  "reason": "Evidence: config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.706 acc / 0.667 F1, a dramatic ~17-point jump over the best singleprofile multimodal result (config_046, 0.537). This identifies multiprofile as the dominant design lever. The aggregation method (avgpool) is the one untested variable within this otherwise proven recipe. Question: config_001 is identical to config_033 except aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer, isolating the effect of a more expressive cross-profile aggregation. Why best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable exploitation of the strongest evidence in the search. If transformer outperforms avgpool, we immediately gain a better configuration; if not, we confirm avgpool is sufficient and can redirect budget to other axes (e.g., RNA encoder or image encoder) without ambiguity. No other available config isolates this question as cleanly."
}

